  - Stripping escape codes alone leaves fragments. Spinners, partial row updates and redrawn prompts depend on text     
    already on screen.[98C
  - The model replays the stream through a grid. It then reads the final rows as text.[34C
  - It is not a full terminal emulator. It handles the sequences the supported runners emit.[28C
[120C
  [1mThe[22m [1mdata[22m [1mmodel[22m[K[104C
  - [38;2;177;185;249mscreen [m([38;2;177;185;249mscreen.go:58[m) holds the grid [38;2;177;185;249mcells[m, the cursor ([38;2;177;185;249mrow[m, [38;2;177;185;249mcol[m), the current [38;2;177;185;249msgr [mand the [38;2;177;185;249mhistory [mslice.[K[11C
  - [38;2;177;185;249mcell [m([38;2;177;185;249mscreen.go:37[m) holds one rune, an [38;2;177;185;249mext [mindex and an [38;2;177;185;249msgr [mstring.[K[49C
  - [38;2;177;185;249mcell.sgr [mkeeps colour codes verbatim, so replay never interprets individual attributes.[K[29C
  - A wide character takes two cells. The second cell holds the sentinel [38;2;177;185;249mcontCh [m([38;2;177;185;249mscreen.go:45[m), which is never written  
    out.[112C
  - Combining marks live in [38;2;177;185;249mscreen.combs[m, and [38;2;177;185;249mcell.ext [mindexes into it. [38;2;177;185;249mcombIdx [mde-duplicates them.[K[21C
  - [38;2;177;185;249mcombMax [mand [38;2;177;185;249mcombsMaxKept [mcap the cost of a stream made only of marks.[K[47C
  - [38;2;177;185;249mblank [mand [38;2;177;185;249mblankRow [m([38;2;177;185;249mscreen.go:175[m) build empty rows.[K[64C
[120C
  [1mSizing[22m [1mthe[22m [1mgrid[22m[K[103C
  - [38;2;177;185;249mnewScreenSized(cols, rows) [m([38;2;177;185;249mscreen.go:156[m) builds the grid at the size the output was drawn at.[K[21C
  - A cols value of 0 or less becomes 80.[79C
  - A rows value of 0 means the ring recorded no height, so [38;2;177;185;249mscreenRows [m(24) is used and [38;2;177;185;249mfixedRows [mis false.[K[13C
  - Rows are clamped to [38;2;177;185;249mscreenMaxRows [m(400).[K[76C
  - [38;2;177;185;249mnewScreen(cols) [mis the wrapper that passes rows of 0.[K[63C
  - The height decides what becomes history. A grid taller than the real terminal keeps rows the session had already    
    scrolled past, and later repaints overwrite them.[67C
  - The comment says this made replay preserve less than no replay.[53C
[120C
  [1mGrowth[22m[K[112C
  - [38;2;177;185;249mgrow(toRow) [m([38;2;177;185;249mscreen.go:198[m) returns at once when the row already exists.[K[44C
  - The comments state that growth applies only when the height is a guess.[45C
  - A recorded height is a ceiling, as on a real terminal. Rows that scroll off are history and cannot be rewritten.    
  - The comment cites a measured case. Growing unconditionally lost 154 of 361 lines, the file listings that collapse to
    [38;2;177;185;249m+31 lines (ctrl+o to expand)[m.[K[87C
[120C
  [1mScrolling[22m [1mand[22m [1mhistory[22m[K[97C
  - Rows that leave the top of the grid are appended to [38;2;177;185;249mhistory[m, oldest first. The transcript is presumably [38;2;177;185;249mhistory     [m
    followed by the final grid rows.[84C
  - [38;2;177;185;249mregion() [m([38;2;177;185;249mscreen.go:112[m) returns the rows a line feed scrolls between. With no region set, that is the whole grid.  
  - [38;2;177;185;249msetRegion(top, bottom) [m([38;2;177;185;249mscreen.go:126[m) implements [38;2;177;185;249mCSI top;bottom r[m, following xterm.js.[K[29C
    - A missing or out-of-range bottom means the last row.[62C
    - A region under two rows is ignored without homing the cursor.[53C
    - A valid region homes the cursor with [38;2;177;185;249mmoveTo(0, 0)[m.[K[64C
  - [38;2;177;185;249mresetRegion() [mrestores the whole grid.[K[78C
  - Each buffer keeps its own region, and the normal buffer's is parked while the alternate buffer is up.[15C
[120C
  [1mCursor[22m [1mstate[22m[K[106C
  - [38;2;177;185;249mwrapNext [mdefers wrapping until the next character. This avoids a blank line after full-width output.[K[16C
  - A carriage return or cursor move cancels [38;2;177;185;249mwrapNext[m.[K[66C
  - [38;2;177;185;249msavedRow[m, [38;2;177;185;249msavedCol [mand [38;2;177;185;249msavedSGR [mimplement DECSC save and restore.[K[51C
  - [38;2;177;185;249mattr [m(an [38;2;177;185;249msgrState[m) is the source that [38;2;177;185;249msgr [mis rendered from. Attributes are set and cleared independently, and a     
    string can only be appended to.[85C
[120C
  [1mAlternate[22m [1mscreen[22m[K[102C
  - [38;2;177;185;249malt[m, [38;2;177;185;249maltCells[m, [38;2;177;185;249maltRow [mand [38;2;177;185;249maltCol [mhold the alternate buffer.[K[57C
  - Whatever a full-screen program draws there is dropped, not added to [38;2;177;185;249mhistory[m.[K[40C
[120C
  [1mHow[22m [1mthis[22m [1mconnects[22m [1mto[22m [1mrestarts[22m [1m([38;2;177;185;249mcarryover.go[m[1m)[22m[K[74C
[120C
  - Scrollback is saved per card id at clean shutdown, and read back on start. It does not survive a crash[14C
    ([38;2;177;185;249mcarryover.go:19-42[m).[K[95C
  - [38;2;177;185;249mcarryDivider [m([38;2;177;185;249mcarryover.go:85[m) marks where one daemon's output ends and the next begins.[K[28C
    - Without it, a join would read as the runner repeating itself.[53C
  - [38;2;177;185;249mcarryCutNotice [mis written into the payload, not the header.[K[57C
    - The format version stays the same, and later generations carry it forward.[40C
  - [38;2;177;185;249mcarryReplayMax [m(4 MB) limits how much pre-restart output one attach replays.[K[40C
    - The comment gives the cost: 23 MB took about 1.4 s to open a terminal.[44C
    - The newest 4 MB costs about 70 ms in the screen model and 300 ms in the browser.[34C
  - [38;2;177;185;249mcarryNotice [m([38;2;177;185;249mcarryover.go:148[m) picks the notice text.[K[63C
    - With a valid nonce, it returns [38;2;177;185;249mcarryLinkNotice[m, which uses OSC 8 [38;2;177;185;249matrium: [mhyperlinks.[K[30C
    - Otherwise it uses the plain [38;2;177;185;249mcarryReplayNotice[m.[K[68C
  - The attach path therefore runs the capped saved bytes through the screen model, then adds the notice at the top.    
[120C
  [1mWhat[22m [1mthe[22m [1mother[22m [1mfiles[22m [1madd[22m[K[94C
[120C
  - [38;2;177;185;249mdocs/activity-design.md [mand [38;2;177;185;249mreaper.go [mare not part of the transcript path.[K[42C
    - The activity doc covers the card badge, which is fed by hooks rather than terminal bytes.[25C
    - The reaper handles liveness. It calls [38;2;177;185;249md.sweepCarryover() [mon its tick, which removes saved scrollback for cards    
      that no longer exist.[93C
[120C
  To complete the picture, read [38;2;177;185;249mapply [mand the rest of [38;2;177;185;249mscreen.go [mpast line 200. That is where escape parsing, [38;2;177;185;249mscrollUp   [m
  and history capture live.[93C
